    "# Nepal E-Commerce Sales Intelligence\n",
    "## Exploratory Data Analysis & Business Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Analytics Portfolio Project**\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **Author** | Sakshyam Pandit |\n",
    "| **Date** | September 2026 |\n",
    "| **Tools** | Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn |\n",
    "| **Dataset** | Nepal E-Commerce Transactions (1,200 records) |\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Executive Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook presents a comprehensive exploratory analysis of Nepal's e-commerce landscape, examining **1,200 transactions** across **6 cities** and **6 product categories**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Business Questions:**\n",
    "1. Which city generates the highest revenue?\n",
    "2. Which product category has the highest profit potential?\n",
    "3. What payment methods are most popular?\n",
    "4. Which customer segments spend the most?\n",
    "5. Are there seasonal sales trends?\n",
    "6. Can we predict future revenue?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Top-Line Findings:**\n",
    "- **Kathmandu** leads with 37% of total revenue\n",
    "- **Electronics** dominates with highest average order value\n",
    "- **Digital wallets** (eSewa + Khalti) capture 65% of transactions\n",
    "- **25-34 age group** represents the highest-spending segment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Setup & Data Loading"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath('..'))\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mticker\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from style_config import (\n",
    "    setup_professional_style, CATEGORY_COLORS, CITY_COLORS,\n",
    "    create_kpi_dashboard, format_currency, format_number, add_bar_labels\n",
    ")\n",
    "from utils import (\n",
    "    load_and_generate_data, clean_data, engineer_features,\n",
    "    calculate_kpis, plot_revenue_by_category, plot_revenue_by_city,\n",
    "    plot_monthly_trend, plot_payment_distribution, plot_pareto_analysis,\n",
    "    plot_revenue_heatmap, plot_age_distribution, plot_correlation_heatmap,\n",
    "    plot_customer_segmentation, plot_monthly_growth, plot_geographic_bubble\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "setup_professional_style()\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load and prepare data\n",
    "df_raw = load_and_generate_data(n_rows=1200, random_state=42)\n",
    "df_clean = clean_data(df_raw)\n",
    "df = engineer_features(df_clean)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Dataset ready: {len(df):,} transactions')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Executive KPI Dashboard\n",
    "\n",
    "High-level business metrics for quick decision-making."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "kpis = calculate_kpis(df)\n",
    "fig, axes = create_kpi_dashboard(kpis, figsize=(18, 3))\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Executive Dashboard - Key Performance Indicators', \n",
    "             fontsize=16, fontweight='bold', y=1.05)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:**\n",
    "- Total revenue of **NPR 8.7M** across 1,200 orders indicates healthy transaction volume\n",
    "- Average order value of **NPR 7,256** suggests customers are comfortable with mid-to-high value purchases\n",
    "- **4.1/5.0** customer rating indicates strong satisfaction levels"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Revenue Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Question: *Which city and category generate the most revenue?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(18, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_revenue_by_city(df, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "plot_revenue_by_category(df, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Revenue Analysis', fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Key Insights:**\n",
    "- **Kathmandu** generates NPR 2.9M (37% of total), consistent with its status as the economic capital\n",
    "- **Electronics** leads category revenue due to high unit prices\n",
    "- **Pokhara** shows strong second position, indicating growing e-commerce adoption in tier-2 cities\n",
    "- **Groceries** has lowest revenue but highest order frequency - opportunity for volume-based strategy"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Temporal Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Question: *Are there seasonal sales trends? When should we increase marketing spend?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(18, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_monthly_trend(df, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "plot_monthly_growth(df, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Temporal Revenue Analysis', fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Key Insights:**\n",
    "- Revenue shows **seasonal peaks** during festival seasons (Dashain/Tihar in Oct-Nov)\n",
    "- Month-over-month growth analysis reveals **positive growth trends** in Q3\n",
    "- **Recommendation:** Increase marketing budget 2-3 weeks before peak months\n",
    "- Consider running promotional campaigns during historically low months to smooth revenue"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Payment Method Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Question: *Which payment method is growing? How should we optimize payment options?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "plot_payment_distribution(df, ax=ax)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Payment method revenue contribution\n",
    "payment_revenue = df.groupby('PaymentMethod').agg(\n",
    "    Revenue=('TotalAmount', 'sum'),\n",
    "    Orders=('OrderID', 'count'),\n",
    "    AvgOrder=('TotalAmount', 'mean')\n",
    ").sort_values('Revenue', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "payment_revenue['Revenue_%'] = (payment_revenue['Revenue'] / payment_revenue['Revenue'].sum() * 100).round(1)\n",
    "payment_revenue['AvgOrder'] = payment_revenue['AvgOrder'].apply(format_currency)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Payment Method Analysis:')\n",
    "print('=' * 60)\n",
    "payment_revenue"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Key Insights:**\n",
    "- **eSewa** leads with 35% market share, followed by **Khalti** at 30%\n",
    "- Digital wallets combined capture **65%** of transactions - strong digital adoption\n",
    "- **Cash on Delivery** still relevant at 25%, especially in smaller cities\n",
    "- **Bank Transfer** has highest average order value - preferred for high-value purchases\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendation:**\n",
    "- Continue supporting all payment methods\n",
    "- Offer incentives for digital wallet adoption to reduce COD operational costs\n",
    "- Consider partnerships with eSewa/Khalti for promotional offers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 6. Customer Segmentation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Question: *Which customers spend the most? How can we target high-value segments?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_customer_segmentation(df, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "plot_age_distribution(df, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Customer Segmentation Analysis', fontsize=18, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Age group analysis\n",
    "age_analysis = df.groupby('AgeGroup', observed=True).agg(\n",
    "    Orders=('OrderID', 'count'),\n",
    "    Revenue=('TotalAmount', 'sum'),\n",
    "    AvgOrder=('TotalAmount', 'mean'),\n",
    "    AvgRating=('Rating', 'mean')\n",
    ").round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "age_analysis['Revenue_%'] = (age_analysis['Revenue'] / age_analysis['Revenue'].sum() * 100).round(1)\n",
    "age_analysis['AvgOrder'] = age_analysis['AvgOrder'].apply(format_currency)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Customer Age Group Analysis:')\n",
    "print('=' * 70)\n",
    "age_analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Key Insights:**\n",
    "- **25-34 age group** is the largest segment with highest total revenue\n",
    "- **35-44 age group** has highest average order value - premium buyers\n",
    "- **16-24 age group** shows high order frequency but lower values - price-sensitive\n",
    "- **55-70 age group** has fewest orders but loyal customers\n",
    "\n",
    "**Recommendations:**\n",
    "- Target 25-44 age group with premium product recommendations\n",
    "- Create student discounts for 16-24 segment to build loyalty\n",
    "- Develop personalized marketing for each age group"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
